<title>HUNGARY: Zalakeramia above issue price - source.</title>
<headline>Zalakeramia above issue price - source.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Global Depositary Receipts (GDRs) in Hungarian tile maker Zalakeramia began to trade in London on Wednesday and were marked above their subscription price of $7.67.</p>
<p>&quot;The issue was $7.67 and now it is trading at $7.88 to $8.30,&quot; one London-based salesman said. &quot;I have seen no volume at all (until 0850 GMT).&quot; One share represent five GDRs.</p>
<p>No information was immediately available on the number of issued shares within the range of 900,000 and 1.2 million shares, but domestic newspaper Napi Gazdasag said foreign investors subscribed 1.428 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
